  "body": "In 2017, LBRY Inc. released the LBRY protocol with the `lbry://@<channel>/<name>` scheme for sharing video/audio in a decentral way. The scheme is well specificed on https://lbry.tech/spec and the scheme is also registered in the IANA list. There are already applications (LBRY Desktop and Odysee Android) that are able to catch the \"lbry\" scheme, but sites like odysee.com and madiator.com are not allowed to let their websites and PWAs register this scheme. It seems reasonable for me to add this scheme to the allowlist.\r\n\r\nWould there be any support for adding this scheme, and if there is some opposition, what are the obstacles?\r\n\r\n```diff\r\nbitcoin\r\nftp\r\nftps\r\ngeo\r\nim\r\nirc\r\nircs\r\n+lbry\r\nmagnet\r\nmailto\r\nmatrix\r\nmms\r\nnews\r\nnntp\r\nopenpgp4fpr\r\nsftp\r\nsip\r\nsms\r\nsmsto\r\nssh\r\ntel\r\nurn\r\nwebcal\r\nwtai\r\nxmpp\r\n```",
